SORT(1)

NAME
     sort - put lines in order

SYNOPSIS
     sort [-nru] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
     Prints the lines of its input in order: digits first, then
     capitals, then small letters.

     -n     order by the number each line starts with, so 9 comes
            before 10
     -r     reverse the order
     -u     print each different line only once

EXAMPLES
     cut -f1 /usr/adm/usage.log | sort
     cut -f1 /usr/adm/usage.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -n

SEE ALSO
     uniq(1), cut(1)
